      "id": 1,
      "text": "John Laurence Jensen, a Danish immigrant, founded Jensen Beach in 1881 by planting pineapples that would later give the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jensen_Beach%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1895, Jensen was called the 'Pineapple Capital of the World,' shipping over a million boxes of fruit each summer season.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jensen_Beach%2C_Florida",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "All Saints Episcopal Church, erected in 1898, stands as the oldest building in both Jensen Beach and Martin County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jensen_Beach%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The annual Pineapple Festival, a long‑standing tradition, honors Jensen Beach’s pineapple past with food, music, and local art.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
